aarch64 #23/#25: apply the checkin init-cache seeds in BOTH libsystem_kernel variants (not dyld-only).

#25 folds task_self/host_self/uid/gid/vchroot from the checkin reply into apple[] and mach_driver_init
seeds the guest caches from them -- but that seeding sat inside #ifdef VARIANT_DYLD, so only the dyld
loader's copy was seeded. libsystem_kernel.dylib (which the guest's own traps use) has its OWN statics
and was never seeded, so it re-RPC'd task_self and uidgid on every process. Moving the seed parse to
the always-compiled block (elf_calls stays dyld-only) seeds the dylib copy too. On fork (applep NULL)
nothing re-seeds; the fork child resets task/host self and re-fetches, and uid/gid/vchroot are
fork-preserved.

This is a general baseline improvement (NOT gated on CIDER_INGUEST_IPC): exec-true RECV 70 -> 59
flag-off (task_self_trap 4->1, uidgid 4->1... i.e. the dylib-side fetches go away), rc=0, soak 8/8.
Combined with the flag it reaches RECV 38. Recommend fork-heavy + login validation before landing in
the prefix. On top of 0054.

